ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T08:43:00Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T08:43:00Z","body":"@leaanthony Can no longer reproduce the issue with this PR on my main project, so looks fixed. 👍 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wailsapp/wails/issues/comments/4610568692/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wailsapp/wails/issues/comments/4610573709","html_url":"https://github.com/wailsapp/wails/issues/5527#issuecomment-4610573709","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wailsapp/wails/issues/5527","id":4610573709,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCact888AAAABEs_FjQ","user":{"login":"Mihara","id":400675,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDY3NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/400675?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara","html_url":"https://github.com/Mihara","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mihara/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T08:43:42Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T08:43:42Z","body":"...ack, that was a misclick, this shouldn't be closed until the fix is in, but now I can't reopen it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wailsapp/wails/issues/comments/4610573709/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wailsapp/wails/issues/comments/4612160835","html_url":"https://github.com/wailsapp/wails/issues/5527#issuecomment-4612160835","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wailsapp/wails/issues/5527","id":4612160835,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCact888AAAABEuf9Qw","user":{"login":"dedo1911","id":1364496,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjQ0OTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1364496?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911","html_url":"https://github.com/dedo1911","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dedo1911/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T12:11:21Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T12:11:21Z","body":"Independent confirmation that #5530 fixes this, plus some diagnostics that might be useful for a regression test.\n\n**Reproduced independently** on a different app/setup, no inspector needed: a Wails v3 app whose Go side `Emit`s an event to the frontend on a timer (every few seconds, so it keeps driving `ExecJS` on the main thread) freezes the same way after ~5–15 min idle — UI completely dead, Go backend fine, no log output, process alive at 0% CPU.\n\nEnvironment: Wails `v3.0.0-alpha.97`, Go `1.26.3`, WebKitGTK `2.52.3`, Ubuntu 24.04, NVIDIA + Wayland. It reproduces on **both** the GTK4/WebKitGTK-6.0 backend and the GTK3/WebKit2GTK-4.1 backend (`-tags gtk3`) — consistent with the offending `fix_signal(SIGUSR1)` being present in both `linux_cgo.c` and `linux_cgo_gtk3.go`.\n\n**Native backtraces at freeze** (gdb) pinpoint the JSC GC ↔ thread-suspend deadlock:\n\nMain (GTK) thread — parked waiting for the GC to grant heap access:\n```\nJSC::Heap::acquireAccessSlow()\nWTF::ParkingLot::parkConditionallyImpl(...)\nWTF::ThreadCondition::timedWait(...)\n___pthread_cond_wait\n... g_main_context_iteration  ->  g_application_run  (cgo)\n```\nJSC \"Collector Thread\" — stuck mid stop-the-world:\n```\nWTF::Thread::suspend(WTF::ThreadSuspendLocker const&)\n__new_sem_wait_slow64  /  do_futex_wait\n```\nThe JSC `Collector Thread` + `HeapHelper` threads spawn exactly at the moment of the freeze; Go goroutine count and RSS stay flat (so this is a native wedge, not a Go-side leak or goroutine pileup). That's precisely the `SA_ONSTACK`-on-`SIGUSR1` corruption #5530 describes — JSC owns SIGUSR1 once it prints `Overriding existing handler for signal 10`, and forcing `SA_ONSTACK` makes its GC suspend handler run on Go's alternate signal stack.\n\n**Fast, deterministic repro** (might be worth a regression test): run with `JSC_collectContinuously=true` so a GC fires immediately — the unfixed alpha.97 build wedges within **~60 seconds** instead of minutes. Non-intrusive detection: `/proc/<pid>/task/<pid>/wchan` then sits permanently on `futex_do_wait` (a single transient sample is just a normal GC handshake; a real wedge is many consecutive).\n\n**Fix confirmed.** Bumping to the #5530 merge commit (`ef782b77`, pseudo-version `v3.0.0-alpha.97.0.20260603100745-ef782b77c892`) and rebuilding:\n- Builds clean, no API changes.\n- Under `JSC_collectContinuously=true` (which wedges the unfixed build in ~60 s), the fixed build runs cleanly for 3+ minutes — the main-thread `wchan` cycles `poll ↔ futex ↔ running` with only transient futex waits, never a sustained wedge.\n\nFor completeness, things I ruled out *before* finding #5530 (all still froze): `JSC_useConcurrentGC=false`, `JSC_SIGNAL_FOR_GC=<n>` (the signal moves but Go masks any signal on its threads), `GODEBUG=asyncpreemptoff=1`, and switching to the GTK3 backend. So #5530's signal-handler change is the correct and sufficient fix.\n\nSince this was closed by a misclick before the fix merged — confirming it's resolved by #5530. Thanks for the quick turnaround! 🙏\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wailsapp/wails/issues/comments/4612160835/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wailsapp/wails/issues/comments/4612790980","html_url":"https://github.com/wailsapp/wails/issues/5527#issuecomment-4612790980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wailsapp/wails/issues/5527","id":4612790980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCact888AAAABEvGaxA","user":{"login":"leaanthony","id":1943904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDM5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1943904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leaanthony","html_url":"https://github.com/leaanthony","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leaanthony/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leaanthony/following{/oth